<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 390 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 390 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 390 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted all 390 million in repos to August 8 and 11 and has now provided liquidity totalling 1.851 billion stg so far on Friday, in response to a forecast money market shortage of two billion pounds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
